{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-87450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $3(7-4x)^{2}+5<-25.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quadratic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(7-4x)^{2}+5 & <-25 \\\\ 3(7-4x)^{2} & <-30 \\\\ (7-4x)^{2} & <-10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(7-4x)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(2)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b723635077024f69582ac7ff67b74ca6fc6d42dc7af98ff5dfde94147680eea"} {"question" "q-87450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\sqrt{10}<x<\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "x<\\sqrt{10}"] ["math" "x>\\sqrt{10}"] ["text" "All real numbers"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve $2(x+7)^{2}+4\\le -6.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quadratic term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+7)^{2}+4 & \\le -6 \\\\ 2(x+7)^{2} & \\le -10 \\\\ (x+7)^{2} & \\le -5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHowever, $(x+7)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x$ because the power $(2)$ is even.\n\nTherefore, there is no solution to the given inequality." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b723635077024f69582ac7ff67b74ca6fc6d42dc7af98ff5dfde94147680eea"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\le -7-\\sqrt{5}"] ["math" "x\\le 2\\sqrt{2}-3"] ["math" "x\\le 7-\\sqrt{10}"] ["text" "All real numbers"] ["text" "No solution"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "No solution"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2(x-2)^{6}-1\\ge 3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the sixth-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{6}-1 & \\ge 3 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{6} & \\ge 4 \\\\ (x-2)^{6} & \\ge 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the sixth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{(x-2)^{6}} & \\ge \\sqrt[6]{2} \\\\ |x-2| & \\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\nx-2\\le -\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x-2\\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le 2-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge 2+\\sqrt[6]{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b723635077024f69582ac7ff67b74ca6fc6d42dc7af98ff5dfde94147680eea"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\le x\\le -4+\\sqrt[6]{2}"] ["math" "x\\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}"] ["math" "x\\le 2-\\sqrt[6]{2}"] ["text" "$x\\le -\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge \\sqrt[6]{2}$"] ["text" "$x\\le 2-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 2+\\sqrt[6]{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-87920" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x\\le 2-\\sqrt[6]{2}\\,$ or $\\,x\\ge 2+\\sqrt[6]{2}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $(x-6)^{2}+4\\ge 11.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quadratic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{2}+4 & \\ge 11 \\\\ (x-6)^{2} & \\ge 7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the square root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{(x-6)^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{7} \\\\ |x-6| & \\ge \\sqrt{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\nx-6\\ge \\sqrt{7}\\,\\text{or}\\,x-6\\le -\\sqrt{7}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-6 & \\ge \\sqrt{7} &  &  & x-6 & \\le -\\sqrt{7} \\\\ x & \\ge \\sqrt{7}+6 &  &  & x & \\le -\\sqrt{7}+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le -\\sqrt{7}+6\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge \\sqrt{7}+6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b723635077024f69582ac7ff67b74ca6fc6d42dc7af98ff5dfde94147680eea"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6-\\sqrt{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278128" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6+\\sqrt{7}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact solution of the inequality $3(x-5)^{4}-4\\ge 23.$\n\n$x\\le ${{field-1}}\n$\\,\\text{or}\\,x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the quartic-degree term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-5)^{4}-4 & \\ge 23 \\\\ 3(x-5)^{4} & \\ge 27 \\\\ (x-5)^{4} & \\ge 9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take the fourth root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[4]{(x-5)^{4}} & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{9} \\\\ |x-5| & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\nx-5\\ge \\sqrt[4]{9}\\,\\text{or}\\,x-5\\le -\\sqrt[4]{9}\n$$\n\nWe can solve each inequality using the usual methods.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-5 & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{9} &  &  & x-5 & \\le -\\sqrt[4]{9} \\\\ x & \\ge \\sqrt[4]{9}+5 &  &  & x & \\le -\\sqrt[4]{9}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\nx\\le -\\sqrt[4]{9}+5\\,\\text{or}\\,x\\ge \\sqrt[4]{9}+5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5b723635077024f69582ac7ff67b74ca6fc6d42dc7af98ff5dfde94147680eea"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5-\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14040763/state.json" "file_sha256" "31f0c94c91bc9cf583a0732a16e0237f5b6a045ea9a959249031595e5f71c444"} {"question" "q-278129" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category"